menu "Tap locator"

    config TAPLOC_SAMPLE_RATE
        int "Microphone sample rate (Hz)"
        default 16000
        help
            One sample is 1/rate seconds of sound travel: 2.1 cm at 16 kHz.
            All boards must use the same rate.

    config TAPLOC_TRIGGER_RATIO
        int "Trigger when a sample exceeds this many times the background level"
        default 12
        help
            Lower hears quieter taps and more false ones.

    config TAPLOC_TRIGGER_MIN
        int "Smallest sample magnitude that can trigger (of 32768)"
        default 200
        help
            Keeps a silent room, where the background level is near zero,
            from triggering on nothing.

    config TAPLOC_BUZZER_GPIO
        int "GPIO the piezo buzzer is on (-1: none, this board only listens)"
        default 1
        range -1 48
        help
            GPIO 1 is pad D0 on the XIAO. Wire a piezo disc or a passive piezo
            buzzer between this pin and GND. A magnetic buzzer or a speaker
            draws more than a pin can give and needs a transistor.

    config TAPLOC_SWEEP_F0
        int "Sweep start (Hz)"
        default 2000

    config TAPLOC_SWEEP_F1
        int "Sweep end (Hz)"
        default 6000
        help
            Must stay under half the sample rate. A wider sweep times more
            sharply; a piezo is loudest between about 2 and 5 kHz. All boards
            must use the same sweep.

    config TAPLOC_SWEEP_MS
        int "Sweep length (ms)"
        default 50
        range 20 64
        help
            A longer sweep is heard further away: doubling it is worth about
            40% more distance.

    config TAPLOC_SWEEP_PERIOD_MS
        int "Average time between this board's sweeps (ms)"
        default 3000
        range 500 60000
        help
            Each gap is random, 25% either side of this. More sweeps track the
            clocks more closely; fewer are quieter and leave more silence for
            hearing taps.

    config TAPLOC_SWEEP_DETECT_DB
        int "A sweep must stand this far above the background (dB)"
        default 13
        range 8 30
        help
            Lower hears sweeps from further away and reports more false ones,
            which the box discards.

    config TAPLOC_BEACON_MS
        int "Time between ESP-NOW timing beacons (ms); 0 switches the radio link off"
        default 250
        range 0 1000
        help
            Boards that hear the same beacon hear it at the same instant, which
            relates their clocks without buzzers. The same radio link carries
            reports to a neighbour that can reach the box. It keeps the Wi-Fi
            radio awake, which costs tens of milliamps. With 0 the boards rely
            on sweeps or calibration taps and the radio sleeps between reports.
            All boards must be on the same channel: see the next setting.

    config TAPLOC_RADIO_CHANNEL
        int "Channel for the ESP-NOW link (0: stay on Wi-Fi and use its channel)"
        default 1
        range 0 13
        depends on TAPLOC_BEACON_MS > 0
        help
            With a channel set, the board leaves its Wi-Fi network and keeps
            its radio on this channel, so every board is certain to be on the
            same one wherever it is. Reports then reach the box through a
            neighbouring board that is on USB or Wendy Net, and the board can
            only be deployed to over USB. All boards must use the same channel.

    config TAPLOC_REPORT_MS
        int "Time between reports to the box (ms)"
        default 5000
        range 500 60000
        help
            The radio sleeps between reports. Taps are still sent at once.

    config TAPLOC_PORT
        int "UDP port the box listens on"
        default 47800

    config TAPLOC_BOX_HOST
        string "Box IPv4 address (empty: find it by broadcast)"
        default ""
        help
            Set this on networks that do not carry broadcast traffic.

endmenu
